# Skill Installation for All Agents

When the user asks to install a skill or plugin, **always install for all three tools**: Cursor, Claude Code, and Codex.

## Installation Process

1. **Run the skills installer with global flag:**
   ```bash
   npx skills add <repo-url> --skill <skill-name> --yes --global
   ```

2. **Fix Claude Code compatibility** (Claude Code may not follow symlinks):
   ```bash
   rm -rf ~/.claude/skills/<skill-name>
   cp -R ~/.agents/skills/<skill-name> ~/.claude/skills/
   ```

3. **Result:** Skill available in:
   - **Cursor** — via `~/.agents/skills/` (or `~/.cursor/plugins/cache/`)
   - **Claude Code** — via `~/.claude/skills/` (real copy)
   - **Codex** — via `~/.agents/skills/` or `~/.codex/skills/`

## Example

For `vercel-react-best-practices` from `https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills`:

```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills --skill vercel-react-best-practices --yes --global
rm -rf ~/.claude/skills/vercel-react-best-practices
cp -R ~/.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices ~/.claude/skills/
```
